        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitcalifornia.com/places-to-visit/sutter-creek/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s Main Street features filigreed balconies of 19th‑century buildings that cantilever over sidewalks, earning it the nickname “Jewel of the Motherlode.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitcalifornia.com/places-to-visit/sutter-creek/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "John Vukovich, a Major League Baseball player, grew up in Sutter Creek and attended Amador High School.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
